I have discovered a way to kill the altar priest in the Gnome Town
(or any other altar priest you want to kill) with almost _NO_ risk.
I'm talking about the priest who guard altars that say "you feel a
strange sense of ..." when you enter.  Since you obviously do not want
to kill prists of your own alignment, I would not advise doing that.
But then again, you can do whatever you like.

<< SPOILER >>

All you need is speed.  A potion or spell from a spellbook will do it,
or of course speed boots or the various other ways to speed yourself
up.  The theory is this: Altar priests will never leave the altar room.
They'll instead stay behind and guard the place.  So here's what you do.
First, convert the altar to your own alignment by sacrificing a 
"larger" creature, like a dwarf, giant ant, Mordor orc, etc. etc. 
This will anger the priest.  The next step is to run away, out of the room.
While you're "speeded," step into the room and stand on the door --
NOT the first step inside the altar.  Only on the opened door.
The angry priest (you must have first made him/her angry) will advance
toward you.  Hit him once, then step away and out of the room.  The
priest will then retreat into the altar room and move to the side, in
order to avoid a wand or missile attack -- much like a shopkeeper or
unicorn will do.  After this, step back onto the door and repeat the
process.  While you're speeded, you will always get an attack and
a retreat move before the priest can hit you.  Repeat until he's dead.

The most dangerous aspect of this plan is that if a priest DOES hit
you, he will most likely summon a bunch of little "a's" - beatles,
giant ants, killer bees, etc.  Then you're in some trouble.  But if
you manage to kill them, they make great sacrifice fuel....

